[38;5;231m⏺[39m Here's the design, in sections. Please tell me if each one looks right before I write it up.

  [1mSection 1: Components and data flow[0m

  - [1mNew [38;5;153msession.js[0m (an ES module next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m). It's the only code that touches the stored ID. It stores [38;5;153m{ userId, [39m
    [38;5;153musername, loggedInAt }[39m as JSON under one key, [38;5;153m"session"[39m. It exports:
    - [38;5;153msetSession({ userId, username })[39m saves the record with a timestamp.
    - [38;5;153mgetSession()[39m returns the record, or [38;5;153mnull[39m if nothing is stored or the stored data is broken (it never throws).
    - [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m is a shortcut: [38;5;153mgetSession()?.userId ?? null[39m.
    - [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m deletes the key, ready for a future logout.
  - [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[39m changes:[0m
    - [38;5;153mlogin(username, password)[39m keeps the same inputs. On success it works out a [38;5;153muserId[39m and returns [38;5;153m{ success: true, [39m
      [38;5;153muser: username, userId }[39m. Until the real API exists, the stub uses the username as the ID, with a comment marking
      the spot where the server's ID goes later.
    - The submit handler calls [38;5;153msetSession(...)[39m after a successful login, and the log line now says who logged in,
      including the ID.
    - It imports from [38;5;153m./session.js[39m.
  - [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[39m:[0m the script tag becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m.
  - [1mLater forms[0m do [38;5;153mimport { getUserId } from "./session.js"[39m and never read localStorage themselves.

  Does that look right? One thing to check: is the username a reasonable stand-in for the ID until the API exists, or do
  you already have a real ID format (numeric, UUID)?

